WEBVTT

00:00:06.988 --> 00:00:18.811
<v Jamie>Oil just cracked one hundred dollars a barrel, and the Energy Department's projecting diesel prices jump thirty-three cents by twenty twenty-seven—which means your supply chain's about to get a masterclass in inflation it didn't sign up for.
  ↳ source: https://www.marketwatch.com/story/diesel-prices-hit-another-record-high-if-youre-shocked-wait-until-you-see-your-grocery-bill-afee7076?mod=mw_rss_topstories

00:00:18.811 --> 00:00:26.279
<v Alex>The Energy Department publishes their forecast through twenty twenty-seven, and diesel up another thirty-three cents by then—that's not a prediction, that's a surrender.
  ↳ source: https://www.axios.com/2026/09/09/energy-department-hikes-2027-diesel-price-outlook

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:34.990
<v Jamie>So the government's basically saying energy risk is no longer a tail event, it's the structural cost of doing business in America for the next three years.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:49.303
<v Maya>Apple's new CEO just dusted off a twenty-five-year-old Steve Jobs playbook—the one where you stand on stage and tell people the iPhone is still the thing, and somehow that counts as innovation. We've gone from inventing the future to reminding people the past still works.

00:00:49.303 --> 00:01:01.126
<v Maya>Automattic's board finally did what boards are supposed to do—they told Matt Mullenweg to take a leave of absence. Against his will. That's the sentence that kills the founder-worship narrative: when the board wins, the founder loses.
  ↳ source: https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/09/automattics-board-forces-ceo-matt-mullenweg-into-leave-of-absence/

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:10.460
<v Alex>Mullenweg announced it on Slack like it was his choice, but governance doesn't work that way. The board forced him out. That's not a sabbatical, that's a legal ejection.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:19.172
<v Maya>AI deepfakes are now good enough that voters can't tell what's real anymore—which means the election just became a trust exercise in institutions we've already stopped trusting.

00:01:19.172 --> 00:01:30.373
<v Jamie>So we've gone from 'fake news' as a political slur to actual fake videos flooding the airwaves, and the only thing standing between democracy and total epistemic collapse is your ability to spot a deepfake.

00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:37.218
<v Alex>Three years from now, when that diesel bill hits your door, you'll remember we all saw it coming and did nothing.

00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:42.196
<v Maya>The forecast was the surrender—we just didn't call it that until it was too late.

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:46.552
<v Jamie>This show is for entertainment and education only — nothing here is investment advice.
